  "_wearableNote": "Four markers come from a wearable or a smart scale rather than a blood panel, and each one is here only because a published interval exists for it. BMI 18.5-24.9 is the WHO normal-weight band (https://www.who.int/health-topics/obesity). Sleep duration 7-9 h is the National Sleep Foundation recommendation for adults 18-64, consistent with the AASM/SRS 7-or-more consensus (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29073412/). Resting heart rate 60-100 bpm is the conventional adult normal; trained endurance athletes sit below it, which is why that marker's on-screen descriptor says so. Blood oxygen 95-100 % is the standard normal on room air. Metrics WITHOUT a published interval, which is steps, HRV and every vendor readiness or recovery score, are deliberately absent: with no normal range there is nothing to be inside or outside of, and inventing one would be the worst thing this app could do."
}
